WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.900 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Our next guest is

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
the United States Secretar
of the Interior.

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:06.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Secretary Deb Haaland.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:08.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here, Secretary.

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:09.709 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's my pleasure.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:10.810 line:92%
Thanks for having me, Seth

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This may or may not
surprise you --

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:16.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are the first secretar
of the Interior

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.150 line:92%
we have ever had on the show

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Well, some reason,

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
I believe that.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:24.090
-Now, I think that people
don't quite understand

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:28.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
what an expansive portfoli
this job has.

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.696 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I certainly didn't.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
What would you tell people
who are watching,

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:34.367 size:88% position:44%
and may be as uneducated
as I am about the job,

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:38.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
what it is that you guys do,
day in and day out?

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:43.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we manage millions
of acres

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:46.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
of public lands,
waters, natural resources

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:50.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the benefit
of the American people.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.719 line:92%
We conserve those resources,

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:57.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that future generations
will have them.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:01:00.960 size:81% position:41%
And we honor the trust
and treaty obligations

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of Indian tribes.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.063 line:92%
-You mentioned Indian tribes

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.998 line:92%
You were, sort of famously

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
and maybe a little bit lately,
for our nation's history,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.904
but you were the first
Native American secretary

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.472 line:92%
in our United States Cabinet

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:13.506 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And was that something

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you were able to proces
in the moment,

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
the historical significanc
of that?

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:22.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, Seth, considering
the fact that I was sworn in

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:25.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
by the very first
woman vice president,

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.520 size:81% position:41% line:92%
also a woman of color,

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
that was really

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.757 size:84% position:42%
probably the best part.
-I'm sorry, Secretary.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to interrupt you
real quick.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a staffer
who fully crawled

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:35.895 size:88% position:44% line:92%
on the carpet behind you

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:39.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it is the greatest thing
I've ever seen.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Sir.

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:43.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sir, we know you're
behind the desk.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:48.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would love to --
Thank you very much.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.276 line:92%
Now, Secretary, be honest.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.245 line:92%
Do you know who that man is?

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.947 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.982 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And...

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
are those someone else's
glasses he's wearing?

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:03.256
-No. We don't have people
sort of sneaking around,

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:05.291 line:92%
so, yes, I know who that i

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:09.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
and thank you
for making light of it, Seth

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:10.797 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I mean, thank you.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:14.300
You know, we've had giant
comedy stars on this show

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not one of them
has thought to have somebody

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.271 line:92%
crawl by in the background

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.240 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you were talking about the
historical significance

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
and also, you know,
it should be noted,

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:26.613 line:92%
you know, for a department

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:30.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
that has a long and,
oftentimes, violent, history

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Native Americans
in this country.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:37.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, violent, that's puttin
it mildly, I think, Seth.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:42.195
I mean, you know, for centuries,
Indians were --

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:47.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we're victims
of genocide, quite frankly

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
since the Europeans came
to this continent

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.839 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and began colonizing

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
Native Americans
in this country.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.943 line:92%
We've been through many eras

00:02:56.943 --> 00:03:02.649
of detrimental federal policies,
assimilation.

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:04.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, my grandmother,
for example,

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
was taken from her home
when she was eight

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sent
to Catholic boarding school.

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:12.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
For five years,
she wasn't able to come home

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:15.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
So those are some of the thing
that we live with

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:20.800
and it's caused generational
trauma to many communities

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I feel like,
with President Biden in office

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:30.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
with his priority of ensurin
that we live up

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
to those trust
and treaty obligations,

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:35.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it's a new era
for Indian country.

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:38.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
I assume,
any time a different party

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:39.919 line:92%
takes over the White House

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
you obviously have a chang
in philosophies

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the department's
different Cabinet member's run

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:48.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I imagine that this is
as much of a 180

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:51.064
as you can imagine,
with what Donald Trump was doing

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:54.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
with his, you know,
Department of the Interior

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
versus what President Bide
is doing.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, Ryan Zinke,
who had your job,

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
had to resign,
due to an ethics scandal.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:04.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was taken over
by an oil and gas lobbyist

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:05.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Trump administration
opened up

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:10.183
a lot of these public land
for oil and gas exploration.

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:12.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
How was the state
of the department

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:15.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
or how did you find it
when you came in?

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I'll tell you, Seth,
I am so proud to be

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:24.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
on a team of career
professionals who have --

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
we have some employees,

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
some career staff here
at the department,

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:31.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have worked here
for 47 years.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:34.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
People have dedicated
their careers

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:36.075 line:92%
to protecting our public lands

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:40.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm thankful that they staye
through those years

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:44.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that they're here,
ready to work and make sur

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:48.488
that we are meeting
the priorities of the president,

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:52.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
making sure that we are goin
to preserve these lands,

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:55.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
conserve our lands
for future generations.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:58.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want everyone's grandkid
to experience

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:03.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
what I've experienced,
you know, on mountain trails

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:07.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
climbing up to the top
of the Washington Monument

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:10.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
All of those things are here
for everyone to enjoy

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:14.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we owe it
to the career professional

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.248 size:81% position:41% line:92%
right here at the DOI.

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:19.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How can your department assis
with the pro-climate agend

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:22.522 line:92%
that the president has laid out?

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:25.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my goodness.
We can do a lot!

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:28.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we just announce
Vineyard Wind.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:34.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's going to be
this tremendous wind project

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:38.204 line:92%
off the coast of Massachusetts

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:41.240 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It'll create 3,600 jobs.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
We want to make sure
that we are --

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:48.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Crackling nearby ]
We have a 30x30 initiative

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
the America the Beautiful
Initiative.

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:55.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're going to conserve 30
of our land and oceans by 2030

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:59.292 size:75% position:38%
make sure that we're
protecting habitat.

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:02.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right now,
we're just on the edge

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:06.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
of celebrating
the Endangered Species Act

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:09.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
The bald eagle
is the highest numbers

00:06:09.469 --> 00:06:11.270 line:92%
that it's been for decades

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:15.174
and we absolutely, I mean,
we have a lot to celebrate

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:17.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we're going to keep
on that trajectory.

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're going to make sure
that climate change

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:23.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a priority for us here
at the DOI

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:24.584 line:92%
and we're working in conjunction

00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:28.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
with many of my colleagues
in other departments

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:30.857 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to make sure that

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:36.796 size:84% position:42%
we are doing our utmost
to turn that around.

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:39.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to ask --
in your role as secretary,

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:42.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you have to sign off
on the social media tweets

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:45.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the Department of the
Interior has been putting out?

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:50.476 size:88% position:44%
-You know, Seth, I want
to give tremendous kudos

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:53.479 line:92%
to my communications department.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:58.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really good
because I don't manage it.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'm a little glad
to hear you say that

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
because here's some
of what you put out.

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:06.225
Here's a photo of some baby owls
and it says,

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:08.227 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Whooo let the kids out?

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:09.629 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Whoo Whoo Whoo!"

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:12.632 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:13.833 line:92%
-Aren't they cute, though?

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:14.600 line:92%
Aren't they just adorable?

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:17.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They are adorable,
but that's besides the point

00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:18.871 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:22.442
We have this -- What do you call
a moose with no name?"

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:23.576 line:92%
Do you know the answer to this

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:26.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Unfortunately, I don't.

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:27.647 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Anonymoose.

00:07:27.647 --> 00:07:29.382 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:31.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the way,
based on you laughing at this,

00:07:31.551 --> 00:07:34.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
that means they're writing
to your sense of humor.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.188 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:37.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, this one
is a photo of a caribou.

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:40.960
I will admit, Secretary, I had
to read this one three times

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
to even get it,
which, for the record,

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:45.665 size:75% position:38%
happens all the time
with my writers here

00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:47.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
and their jokes,
so I'm not judging.

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:52.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, "Even when you're alone
we caribou-t you."

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:54.907 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"We caribou-t you."

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:59.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, I want to give peopl
a little bit of leeway

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:00.980 size:78% position:39% line:92%
to express themselves

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
on social media.

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:04.050 line:92%
-Well, you do that enough

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you end up with a writer
named Mike Scollins.

00:08:06.385 --> 00:08:09.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
That's what happened to me

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:10.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you do not
want that to happen.

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:14.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, I want to end
by mentioning this.

00:08:14.393 --> 00:08:17.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am married
to an incredible woman

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:21.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was born
and raised in New Mexico

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:23.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the greatest states
in the Union,

00:08:23.903 --> 00:08:27.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I'd never been to,
and, now, I go to all the time

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:31.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
It's a "Land of Enchantment.

00:08:31.444 --> 00:08:33.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I guess my question is,
every time I go,

00:08:33.446 --> 00:08:38.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
the only downside is I hav
to stay with my in-laws

00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:41.153 line:92%
and can I crash with you?

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:41.988 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:41.988 --> 00:08:43.823 line:92%
-Yes, you're welcome any time.

00:08:43.823 --> 00:08:45.157 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:46.959 line:92%
-I really appreciate that.

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:49.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
Secretary, it has been
a pleasure talking with you.

00:08:49.896 --> 00:08:53.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
Keep up the great work and
hopefully, we'll see you again

00:08:53.065 --> 00:08:54.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks so much.
Thanks for having me.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your staff member,
is he still in the room?

00:08:56.235 --> 00:08:57.837 line:92%
Does he want to wave goodbye

00:08:57.837 --> 00:08:59.906 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:01.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does he know he's going
to be a meme?

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:04.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because maybe
you should let him know.

00:09:04.076 --> 00:09:04.677 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.677 --> 00:09:06.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks so much.
-It might be better
coming from you.

00:09:06.612 --> 00:09:08.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Thanks, Seth.

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:12.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
Good to be here.
-Thank you. All the best.

